{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 201 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d04550f5d797626ad0d0ed7517b458f68ad0f0e51cf339395d05b7646765b7ba" :edb/db-before-t 200 :edb/db-after-t 201 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533513 50 #inst "2026-10-11T05:21:45.443Z" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186124575 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406728 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186124575 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406730 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186124575 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406731 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186124580 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406727 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186124580 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406729 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186125235 1068 #edb/ref 17592186123980 13194139533513 17592186045585 false] [17592186125235 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406726 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186125235 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186125235 1071 "Find $f(x, y, z)$ such that $∇f(x, y, z) = F(x, y, z)$, where $F(x, y, z) = (\\cos z + y\\cos x)i + \\sin xj - x\\sin zk$." 13194139533513 17592186045585 false] [17592186125235 1071 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,j-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,k.$" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186125235 1074 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z & =-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406691 1081 "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406691 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406691 1084 #uuid "03292879-7e19-58c5-bf30-9a82b7757e44" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406692 1081 "f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy+C" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406692 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406692 1084 #uuid "03fb1154-e9d5-5abf-a426-4de833dd30db" 13194139533513 17592186045585 true] [17592186406693 1081 "f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{